# Pins the bug that started the syntax-manifest project: an editor grammar
# copy-pasted from Rust's, coloring keywords TypR has never had while the
# real keywords it does have (opaque, module, record, interface, ...) went
# uncolored. None of the words below should carry any special scope — they
# must fall through to plain identifiers (lowercase) or PascalCase aliases
# (uppercase), exactly like any other undeclared name.
impl trait struct enum where mut pub continue Option Result List Matrix Some None Ok Err

# Same for operators: none of these compounds exist in the tokenizer, so
# each must resolve to its real, shorter components instead of being colored
# as one (invented) operator.
a |>> b
a $$ b
a @@ b
a ++ b
a -- b
a ** b
